Rule 10. Format of Pleadings, Motions and Other Papers.
(a) Size and Format. Filings and attachments must:
(1) be of 8 ½ x 11 inch size;
(2) be plainly legible, whether keyed, typed, handwritten, or duplicated;
(3) have at least 1 inch margins;
(4) be no less than 12 point font;
(5) be consecutively numbered;
(6) be double-spaced, except for quoted material;
(7) use footnotes sparingly; and
(8) be paper-clipped or otherwise attached to facilitate scanning.
(b) Facsimile Filings. 
(1) Prior Authorization for Facsimile Filing. The clerk’s office does not accept filings
by facsimile without prior authorization from the court. 
(2) Filing Date. The filing date is the date the clerk’s office adequately receives the
transmission.
